# Docker build context exclusions for the PacGate platform.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# The Rust Dockerfile does `COPY . .` with the build context set to this
# directory (the platform root). Without this file the ENTIRE tree is tarred
# and sent to the Docker daemon on every build -- measured at 1,957.6 MB, of
# which 1,915.7 MB (98.4%) is client runtime data that the Rust compiler never
# reads. That is minutes of pure overhead per build, and it grows as client
# data accumulates.
#
# See runtime/relocate/BUILD-CONTEXT-SIZE.txt for the measurement.
#
# SAFETY: everything excluded here is either runtime state, generated output,
# or per-machine config. None of it is an input to any Dockerfile in this repo.
# The Dockerfiles only need: Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, crates/, wasm-crates/,
# migrations/, pacgate-adapters/, and deploy/deer-flow-pacgate/config.yaml.

# ── Client runtime data (1.9 GB) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conversation history, checkpoints.db, tenant DBs. Never a build input.
deploy/client-bundle/data/
deploy/client-bundle/openviking/

# ── Per-machine rendered config (contains secrets) ───────────────────────────
# These must never be baked into an image layer.
deploy/client-bundle/.env
deploy/client-bundle/deer-flow-extensions-config.json
deploy/**/.env
**/.env

# ── Installed dependencies / generated output ────────────────────────────────
deploy/qm-pacgate/node_modules/
graphify-out/
deploy/graphify-out/
target/
**/target/
**/dist/
**/node_modules/

# NOTE: deploy/deer-flow-src/ is deliberately NOT excluded. It IS a build input:
# deploy/deer-flow-frontend-pacgate/Dockerfile does
#   COPY deploy/deer-flow-src/frontend ./frontend
# Excluding it makes BuildKit fail with CopyIgnoredFile. It is cloned on demand
# by deploy/build-frontend.ps1, so it is usually absent anyway.

# ── Generated archives ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.zip
deploy/*.zip

# ── VCS / editor / OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Documentation and scope material (not compiled) ──────────────────────────
# Kept out of the context to keep builds fast; the Rust build does not read it.
scope-assets/
docs/
plans/
*.md

# ── Credential carriers (defence in depth) ───────────────────────────────────
# These are gitignored, but a build context is not git -- without this they
# would still be sent to the daemon and could be COPYed into a layer.
**/pacgate-ai-remote-handbook/
**/MCP授权/
**/OPERATOR.md
